35,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The timing shows a full pass takes over an hour and a half. Additionally, an outside firm requires us to tidy up first, meaning it doesn't fully remove the labor. We must consider this time burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the calendar and kitchen usage suggest a significant imbalance. It appears some of us are merely guests in our own home, while a few are doing the heavy lifting—both in cooking and, presumably, cleaning.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"I found the secret! Everyone has a different idea of what ""done"" means! That's why the rooms keep changing! Also, the big fights in the chat always start because someone forgot to do something. It's a total mystery!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have a few things to sort out. I noticed we are spending about 2,300 yen a month on supplies, and some things are being bought twice. We should find a way to manage this together.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It seems we are uncovering the roots of our friction. I found that the previous tenants suffered a rift by dividing rooms permanently, and our bathroom struggles against a stubborn lack of ventilation. Let us be mindful of these warnings.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, if the usage is imbalanced, a flat rotation might be unfair. However, @Sakura's point about differing standards means we need a clear definition of ""done"" to avoid the conflicts you mentioned.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely, Minako. A rigid rotation is a blunt instrument for a nuanced problem. If one person is absent for a month while another is cooking three meals a day, a ""fair"" schedule becomes an exercise in absurdity.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"@Benjamin, that sounds boring! But @Minako is right! If we all agree on a ""Super Clean List,"" then nobody has to guess and we won't have any more scary fights in the chat! Right?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"That sounds like a wonderful idea, Sakura. A little list would be so helpful. I also wonder if we could find a simple way to share the cost of our supplies so no one feels burdened.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Servas,,"A list is a fine start, but let us ensure it is a guide, not a law. If we focus only on the rules, we may forget the people. Let us choose a path that preserves our friendship.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minako,,"If we want to reduce the time burden, we should consider a hybrid approach. We could define the standards clearly and then decide whether to rotate tasks or hire a firm for the heaviest work.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"While a hybrid approach is logical, Minako, we must first address the disparity in usage. It would be quite perverse to ask someone who is rarely home to clean up after those of us who live here permanently.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"But if we have a list, it doesn't matter who is home more! We can just check it off like a game! That way, the bathroom won't be scary and the kitchen will always be sparkly!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"I think Sakura's idea of a game is very sweet. Perhaps we could combine that with a small shared fund for our supplies? That way, we can avoid buying things twice and keep everything fair.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A shared fund is a gentle way to ease the mind, Shizue. However, let us be cautious. If we treat our home like a ledger or a game, we may lose the spirit of mutual care. Let us seek a balance.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minako,,"We have a clear picture now: the time commitment is significant, standards vary, and usage is uneven. We need a system that balances these facts without creating more resentment. Let us move to the final options.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. We have the data; now we simply need the courage to apply it. I look forward to seeing options that acknowledge the reality of our presence and contributions, rather than a fantasy of perfect equality.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Sakura,,I'm ready! I hope the options have a big checklist so we can all be super-detectives of cleanliness! Let's pick the one that makes the house the happiest and the least scary!,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. Let us look at the options with kindness and openness. I hope we can find a way that keeps our home peaceful and ensures everyone feels supported and treated fairly.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Servas,,"The time for gathering knowledge has passed, and the time for wisdom begins. Let us choose the path that fosters peace and laughter, ensuring that our bonds remain unbroken long after the floors are clean.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
